<title>USA: Transact in $17 mln UK post office pact.</title>
<headline>Transact in $17 mln UK post office pact.</headline>
<dateline>WALLINGFORD, Conn. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransAct Technologies Inc said on Friday that it has entered an agreement with a division of computer maker ICL to provide printers for the British postal service.</p>
<p>TransAct said it will deliver the printers from the first quarter of 1997 to the fourth quarter of 1998. TransAct will receive $17 million for the job, spokeswoman Diane DeMartino said.</p>
<p>TransAct, an 80 percent-owned subsidiary of Tridex Corp, said the order brings its current total backlog to $39 million. ICL is majority owned by Fujitsu Ltd.</p>
</text>
